  <title>Cat FAQ</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: dark;
      --bg: #0b1020;
      --panel: #121a2d;
      --panel-strong: #18223b;
      --border: #31415f;
      --text: #edf2ff;
      --muted: #b2bfd9;
      --accent: #7dd3fc;
      --accent-strong: #38bdf8;
      --shadow: 0 20px 45px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: 100vh;
      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: var(--text);
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at top, rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.14), transparent 28%),
        linear-gradient(180deg, #0b1020 0%, #090d18 100%);
    }

    .skip-link {
      position: absolute;
      left: 1rem;
      top: -3rem;
      z-index: 10;
      padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      background: var(--text);
      color: #08101f;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .skip-link:focus {
      top: 1rem;
    }

    main {
      width: min(100% - 2rem, 56rem);
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 4rem 0 5rem;
    }

    .hero {
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
      padding: 2rem;
      border: 1px solid rgba(125, 211, 252, 0.2);
      border-radius: 1.5rem;
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(24, 34, 59, 0.96), rgba(18, 26, 45, 0.92));
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
      line-height: 1.1;
    }

    .hero p {
      margin: 0;
      max-width: 42rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }

    .faq-list {
      display: grid;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .example {
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 1.25rem;
      overflow: hidden;
      background: rgba(18, 26, 45, 0.94);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    .question {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 1rem;
      width: 100%;
      padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem;
      border: 0;
      background: transparent;
      color: var(--text);
      font: inherit;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-align: left;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .question:hover {
      background: rgba(125, 211, 252, 0.08);
    }

    .question:focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--accent);
      outline-offset: -3px;
    }

    .icon {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      display: inline-grid;
      place-items: center;
      width: 2rem;
      height: 2rem;
      border: 1px solid rgba(125, 211, 252, 0.28);
      border-radius: 999px;
      color: var(--accent);
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      transition: transform 0.2s ease, background-color 0.2s ease;
    }

    .question[aria-expanded="true"] .icon {
      transform: rotate(45deg);
      background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.12);
    }

    .details {
      padding: 0 1.25rem 1.25rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(49, 65, 95, 0.75);
    }

    .details p {
      margin: 1rem 0 0;
    }

    .details[hidden] {
      display: none;
    }

    @media (max-width: 40rem) {
      main {
        width: min(100% - 1rem, 56rem);
        padding-top: 2rem;
      }

      .hero,
      .question,
      .details {
        padding-left: 1rem;
        padding-right: 1rem;
      }
    }

    @media (forced-colors: active) {
      .hero,
      .example,
      .icon {
        border-color: ButtonText;
      }

      .hero,
      .example {
        background: Canvas;
        box-shadow: none;
      }

      body,
      .question,
      .details,
      .hero p {
        color: CanvasText;
      }

      .question:focus-visible {
        outline-color: Highlight;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to main content</a>

  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
      <h1 id="page-title">Cat FAQ</h1>
      <p>Quick answers about feline behavior, care, and communication. Each question starts collapsed, so you can open only what you want to read.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-list" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about cats">
      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-1" id="question-1">
          Why do cats purr?
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-1" hidden>
          <p>Cats often purr when they feel content, but purring can also be a way to self-soothe when they are stressed, injured, or seeking comfort from people they trust.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-2" id="question-2">
          How much sleep do cats need?
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-2" hidden>
          <p>Most adult cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day. Kittens and senior cats may sleep even more because their bodies need extra recovery and growth time.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-3" id="question-3">
          Why do cats knead soft blankets?
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-3" hidden>
          <p>Kneading is a comforting behavior that starts in kittenhood during nursing. Adult cats may keep doing it when they feel safe, relaxed, and especially cozy.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-4" id="question-4">
          Do indoor cats need enrichment?
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-4" hidden>
          <p>Yes. Indoor cats benefit from scratching posts, climbing spaces, toys, window views, and regular play sessions that let them stalk, chase, and pounce safely.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-5" id="question-5">
          Why do cats flick their tails?
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-5" hidden>
          <p>Tail movement is a clue to mood. A gentle upright tail can signal friendliness, while quick flicking or thumping often suggests irritation, overstimulation, or focused attention.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    const questions = document.querySelectorAll(".question");

    questions.forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const details = document.getElementById(button.getAttribute("aria-controls"));
        const isExpanded = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";

        button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));
        details.hidden = isExpanded;
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
